    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0458" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v05/pg432"/>

                <head>213. Memorandum for the Record, by the President’s Staff Secretary
                        (Goodpaster)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d213-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1955</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President told me just after a phone call to Sir Anthony Eden at 10:30 on
                    July 21 that Sir Anthony had asked him how soon he might be ready to come to
                    some kind of agreement about offshore procurement of military items for Iraq
                    (and perhaps other mid-East countries).</p>
                <p>The President had indicated to Sir Anthony that he thought it would be possible
                    to do some of this but the amount would have to be studied.</p>
                <p>Sir Anthony asked the President what General Gruenther had thought of the
                    disarmament scheme relating to NATO, and the <pb facs="0459" n="433"
                        xml:id="pg433"/> President said he told Sir Anthony that his thought ran
                    more in terms of an “over-all” arrangement.</p>
                <closer><signed>A.J. Goodpaster<anchor n="2" xml:id="d213-f2"/><lb/>Colonel, CE, US
                        Army</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
